  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Differentiated HIV Services for Key Populations in Malaysia - Malaysia (01-Jul-2019-30-Jun-2022)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaysia, HIV, Malaysian AIDS Council (MAC)This program has the following goals: To transition the Community Case Management Model to domestic funding with a view  adoption as the national mechanism for delivery of HIV services among KP.  To strengthen the capacity of civil society organistions and community-based organisations in HIV response towards achieving the 90-90-90 targets by 2020 and ending AIDS by 2030. The objectives of this program are: To increase the rate of uptake of HIV testing among key populations.  To increase the rate of case finding among key populations.  To increase enrolment in ART among PLHIV from  key populations.  To increase rate of ART adherence among key populations living with HIV</narrative>
  </description>
